VALUES (46581, 'tt0071359', NULL, 'Immoral Tales', 'Contes immoraux', 'movie', 1974, 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/dFPQD3e5uonv7bKTYsi7TqtKxYx.jpg', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/lv7bRurrhBo3vjcwJNztb2ZkDu9.jpg', 'Four erotic tales from various historical eras. The first, ''The Tide'', is set in the present day, and concerns a student and his young female cousin stranded on the beach by the tide, secluded from prying eyes. ''Therese Philosophe'' is set in the nineteenth century, and concerns a girl being locked in her bedroom, where she contemplates the erotic potential of the objects contained within it. ''Erzsebet Bathory'' is a portrait of the sixteenth-century countess who allegedly bathed in the blood of virgins, while ''Lucrezia Borgia'' concerns an incestuous fifteenth-century orgy involving Lucrezia, her brother, and her father the Pope.', NULL, NULL, 8.1907, 5.9, 0, 10.01, '2026-10-17 04:47:13', '2026-10-17 04:47:13')
